  "dom_id": "step-q95450",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=4\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =4(-{csch}^{2}⁡x)-(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4{csch}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
